## Team building through the power of rhythm

Looking for something different for your next corporate event or staff development day? Then look no further, because Rhythm Culture offers high-energy African drumming and dance workshops that get everyone involved, laughing and connecting.

So forget the usual team building activities! Instead, our interactive corporate drumming workshops offer a refreshing way to bring people together. Through African drumming, singing, movement and teamwork, your group will create something amazing.

Everyone gets hands-on with an African drum, such as the [djembe](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Djembe). Our professional facilitators then guide the group through exciting rhythms, interactive activities and collaborative challenges. As the session develops, individual rhythms come together to create a powerful group performance.

### Break down barriers at work

Most importantly, it’s a fantastic way to break down workplace barriers, encourage communication and build connections between colleagues. Whether you’re bringing together a small team or a large corporate event, we create an experience that gets everyone participating.
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}

{% section tone="grey" %}
*Why drumming works*

## The benefits of African drumming for team building

Drumming is more than a fun activity. In fact, it builds the same skills that strong teams rely on every day.

{% columns layout="equal" align="top" %}
{% column %}
### Connection & team bonding

Drumming together creates an immediate sense of connection. That’s because everyone contributes to the group, regardless of their position or role. As a result, it’s a wonderful way to break down barriers and build stronger workplace relationships.
{% /column %}

{% column %}
### Communicate & collaborate

A successful drumming ensemble relies on listening, responding and working together. So participants learn to pay attention to one another. They also see how individual contributions support the bigger picture.
{% /column %}

{% column %}
### Creativity & problem solving

Through rhythm games, musical challenges and group activities, teams explore new ways of thinking and working together. In addition, everyone gets the chance to contribute ideas and step outside their usual roles.
{% /column %}

{% column %}
### Stress relief & workplace wellbeing

Drumming is physical, energising and lots of fun! What’s more, the mix of movement, music and laughter provides a welcome break from everyday workplace pressures. It also gives colleagues a chance to relax and enjoy themselves together.
{% /column %}

{% column %}
### Confidence & collective achievement

There is something incredibly rewarding about creating music as a group. Consequently, participants feel the satisfaction of achieving something together. Finally, they build confidence and celebrate their collective success.
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}
{% /section %}

{% section tone="dark" %}
## What to expect from a Rhythm Culture team building workshop

Every workshop builds from a playful warm-up to a powerful group performance. Here’s how a typical session unfolds.

- **A rhythmic welcome:** First, we surprise your group with the sound of African drums as they enter the room. Participants find their seats, pick up a drum and start exploring their rhythm. So everyone is involved from the very beginning!
- **Getting into the groove:** Next, we show everyone how to get the most out of their drums. Then fun rhythmic games and interactive team building activities help participants warm up, listen and connect.
- **Call & response:** After that, our facilitators introduce lively call-and-response rhythms, layering different parts over a high-energy groove. As a result, everyone learns to listen, respond and contribute to the ensemble.
- **The power of teamwork:** We introduce traditional West African rhythms and play them together in unison. Next, we split the group into sections and each one learns a different part. When we bring everything together, the result shows the power of cooperation.
- **Creating something amazing together:** Now it’s time to get creative! The group turns the rhythms they’ve learnt into their own piece of music. With a few surprises along the way, we build towards an exciting finale that celebrates everyone’s achievement.
{% /section %}

{% columns layout="equal" align="center" %}
{% column %}
*Bring everyone together · Have fun · Learn something new*

## Your team building workshop at a glance

- **Get hands-on:** Everyone receives a West African drum. Then our facilitators introduce the instruments and teach some simple rhythms.
- **Explore rhythm:** Then rhythm games, call-and-response activities and musical challenges help participants listen, communicate and work together.
- **Bring it together:** Next, we combine the individual rhythms into a synchronised drumming ensemble. This is where the magic happens!
- **Add song & dance:** Depending on your event, we can also add traditional songs, African dance and energetic movement activities.
- **Celebrate:** Finally, the workshop builds to a shared musical moment that the whole team will remember.
- **Group size:** Small teams through to large conferences with hundreds of people
- **Venue:** Indoors or outdoors, anywhere in Australia
- **Experience:** None needed, because every activity suits complete beginners

